Full Solution Breakdown (Hash Map One-Pass):
- Time Complexity: O(n) because we traverse the list of n elements exactly once, and each lookup in the hash map takes O(1) time.
- Space Complexity: O(n) auxiliary space to store at most n elements in the hash map.

Python:
```python
class Solution:
    def twoSum(self, nums: list[int], target: int) -> list[int]:
        prevMap = {}
        for i, n in enumerate(nums):
            diff = target - n
            if diff in prevMap:
                return [prevMap[diff], i]
            prevMap[n] = i
        return []
```
